        "original_id": "2aa0951e-5716-56b1-9139-881635a88f6e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Groups: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", \"She's My Kind of Girl\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946 and is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of the Swedish music group ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- \"Money, Money, Money\" is a song recorded by the Swedish pop group ABBA.\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- \"She's My Kind of Girl\" is a song written and performed by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus.\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus later became famous as members of ABBA.\n- The song \"That's Me\" was released as a single in Japan the year after its original release to promote ABBA's album \"Arrival\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" was released with \"Money, Money, Money\" as its B-side.\n- \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
